# This repository holds generated course pages and nothing else. It is written
# by tools/build_public.py in the course's private repository; do not edit files
# here, because the next publish overwrites them.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.tmp

# Deliberately NOT under Foreman's synced-ignores block. A rules sync wrote that block
# here on 30 August 2026, carrying internal process language into a world-readable
# repository; init_project.py now requires a CLAUDE.md before it will write to a folder,
# so this repository is skipped. Keep these entries local.
_scratch/
~$*
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# NOTHING BUT COURSE PAGES. A workspace rules sweep committed tools/gitcommit.sh -
# 362 lines of internal build tooling, with workspace paths and internal rule numbers -
# and a stray git lock file into this world-readable repository on 31 August 2026, and
# it was pushed. It is the second time a sweep has written into this repo; the first
# wrote its own ignore block, which is what the note above is about. The publisher's
# allowlist cannot stop this, because a sweep commits directly and never runs the
# publisher. So the ignore list refuses the two directories a sweep reaches for.
tools/
_to_delete/
_scratch/
_held/
